y of sessions and meeting other runners---I enjoy being part of a running community and the way the club drives me to be a better runner.---The sense of community and the support from other club members.---Having regular training sessions in my diary. Meeting other people to run with---Routine and accountability for---Structure to my runs, PB’s, meeting new friends and being part of a community.---Great atmosphere, experienced coaches, wide variety of different runs every week---Lots! Especially running together, friendliness of the club, chance to get fitter and to take part in more events.---Becoming a better runner and meeting new people---Support from coaches and other runners---Friendly runners of all abilities, coached sessions, very well organised, club champs.---Awesome vibes, varied workouts, proximity---Welcoming atmosphere and competitive spirit---Being part of a group. All the members are very friendly and welcoming as are the coaches.---Focussed sessions and meeting new people.---Running with other people/meeting new people who also like to run---Doing runs I wouldn’t otherwise do on my own---Coached sessions lets me do training that i wouldnt do on my own---Meeting new people who are into running at all levels; the sense of community; accountability; the training support; hearing information about running events; feeling part of a group; being made to feel so welcome.---The amazing community of runners, the all inclusive nature of the club where everyone is made to feel welcome, the Thursday sessions which are extremely well planned.---Social running---the atmosphere---Having sessions that form part of my wider running programme.---The community and accountability of running with others, lovely people all round, regular structured opportunity for running, social events---Place to train locally---How welcoming everyone has been---The friendships I've made---Structured training, welcoming environment for all abilities, new friends---The training session 